//! A schema-6 bank file holding the layouts schema 7 converts on load (code
//! review of 2026-09-12). `ew_ridge` kept each target's cross-moments raw,
//! `E[z·y]`, in three places -- the live accumulators, the `session_shrink`
//! twin and every snapshot in a `window`'s ring -- and schema 7 keeps them
//! centred (N1). `holt` gained each target's clock since its last
//! observation (C22). The third conversion, `bocpd`'s run sums (C23), is in
//! `state_schema6.rs`'s `bo` spec.
//!
//! Frozen bytes for the reasons `state_schema6.rs` gives, generated by the
//! last schema-6 build from the stream `frame` reproduces and the specs the
//! file carries. A conversion from raw to centred moments keeps the numbers
//! and not the bits, so the `ew_ridge` specs are held to `1e-12` against a
//! bank built afresh here; `holt`'s conversion adds a clock that starts at
//! zero and moves nothing else, so `ho` is held to the bit, as
//! `state_schema6.rs` holds its unconverted specs.
//!
//! These tests passed trivially before schema 7 existed, when the build read
//! its own layout. They test the converter, not the findings.

